From 92aecc4bbf85cf684c910e671f5de8a3ca95debe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 23:19:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] misc: bq5105x_detect: don't force ambient backlight on
 wireless dock
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Placing the watch on the wireless charging dock left the backlight dimly
lit even when the screen was supposed to be off. This did not happen on
battery or over the USB debug lines.

When the dock is detected, bq5105x_detect broadcasts a
DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKON notification on the wakeup_source_notify chain.
On the stock (WearOS) firmware this drives an "ambient display while
docked" feature via three consumers: panel-minnow forces
DISPLAY_AMBIENT_ON, m4sensorhub_als keeps the light sensor feeding the
backlight while charging, and leds-lm3535 re-enables the LED for
ALS-while-charging and applies a MIN_DOCK_BVALUE brightness floor. USB
and battery never generate a dock event, which is why the symptom was
dock-only.

On AsteroidOS display and backlight policy is owned by userspace (mce),
so drop the display-wake dock broadcast. All three mechanisms are gated
on that single event, so this disables the forced ambient backlight
entirely. Charging/dock status that userspace needs is still reported in
the same function via power_supply_changed() and switch_set_state(),
which are independent of the display-wake broadcast.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AsteroidOS-specific policy]

Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c b/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
index 37cbdcaa11ce..b8889b551622 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/bq5105x_detect.c
@@ -215,11 +215,20 @@ static void bq5105x_detect_report(struct bq5105x_detect *chip, bool docked)
 {
 	if (chip->reported_docked != docked) {
 		dev_dbg(&chip->pdev->dev, "report docked=%d\n", docked);
-#ifdef CONFIG_WAKEUP_SOURCE_NOTIFY
-		wakeup_source_notify_subscriber(docked
-						? DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKON
-						: DISPLAY_WAKE_EVENT_DOCKOFF);
-#endif
+		/*
+		 * Do NOT broadcast the display-wake dock event. On the stock
+		 * (WearOS) firmware this drives an "ambient display while
+		 * docked" feature: the panel (panel-minnow), the light sensor
+		 * (m4sensorhub_als, ALS-while-charging) and the backlight
+		 * (leds-lm3535, dock brightness floor) all keep a dim always-on
+		 * display lit whenever the wireless charger is present. On
+		 * AsteroidOS display/backlight policy is owned entirely by
+		 * userspace (mce), so this only manifests as the backlight
+		 * refusing to switch off while the watch sits on the dock.
+		 * Charging/dock status is still reported to userspace below via
+		 * power_supply_changed() and switch_set_state(), which are
+		 * independent of the display-wake broadcast.
+		 */
 		chip->reported_docked = docked;
 		power_supply_changed(&chip->charger);
 		switch_set_state(chip->sdev, docked);
